    "title": "Section",
    "content": "**Primary source:** The Smalcald Articles by Martin Luther\n\n**Source:** BookOfConcord.org, public-domain Book of Concord text\n\nTreats of the Sublime Articles Concerning the Divine Majesty, as:\n\n \n\nArticle I - The Nature of God\n\nI. That Father, Son, and Holy Ghost, three distinct persons\nin one divine essence and nature, are one God, who\nhas created heaven and earth.\n\nArticle II - The Father\n\nII. That the Father is begotten of no one; the Son of the Father; the Holy Ghost\nproceeds from Father and Son.\n\nArticle III - The Son\n\nIII. That not the Father nor the Holy Ghost but the Son became man.\n\nArticle IV - The Work of Salvation\n\nIV. That the Son became man in this manner, that He was conceived, without\nthe cooperation of man, by the Holy Ghost, and\nwas born of the pure, holy [ and always] Virgin\nMary. Afterwards He suffered, died, was buried,\ndescended to hell, rose from the dead, ascended\nto heaven, sits at the right hand of God, will\ncome to judge the quick and the dead, etc., as\nthe Creed of the Apostles, as well as that of St. Athanasius,\nand the Catechism in common use for children, teach.\n\nConcerning these articles there is no contention or dispute, since we on both\nsides confess them. Therefore it is not necessary now to treat\nfurther of them."
